## Type casting

A cast convert a value of a type to another type and use the following notation `T(value)` where `T` is the target type as in `int32(2)`.
```
<target_type>(<val>)
```

In the example, `a` has type `int32` and is converted to a `float32` when being returned.

All type conversions are explicit in GX.

```code:main
package main

func Main() float32 {
    a := int32(2)
    return float32(a)
}
```
